1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:04,311
What if World War Three wasn't fought with nukes, but with time itself?

2
00:00:04,361 --> 00:00:08,259
In Tenet, an unnamed CIA agent, known only as The Protagonist,

3
00:00:08,279 --> 00:00:15,146
survives a brutal siege at a Kyiv opera house, where a mysterious masked soldier with an orange trinket saves

4
00:00:15,166 --> 00:00:18,260
his life, using a bullet that flies backward.

5
00:00:18,310 --> 00:00:24,331
After passing a lethal loyalty test, he is recruited into a secret organization called Tenet.

6
00:00:24,381 --> 00:00:29,725
His mission: stop inversion, a technology from the future that reverses an object's entropy,

7
00:00:29,745 --> 00:00:31,977
so it moves backward through time.

8
00:00:32,027 --> 00:00:37,019
The man behind it in the present is Andrei Sator, a ruthless Russian oligarch,

9
00:00:37,039 --> 00:00:41,465
receiving inverted gold and instructions from future antagonists.

10
00:00:41,515 --> 00:00:48,149
Their goal is to assemble the Algorithm, a nine-part doomsday device capable of inverting the entire planet and

11
00:00:48,169 --> 00:00:49,618
wiping out the past.

12
00:00:49,668 --> 00:00:54,182
To reach Sator, The Protagonist teams up with a sharp handler named Neil,

13
00:00:54,202 --> 00:00:56,439
and Sator's estranged wife, Kat.

14
00:00:56,489 --> 00:01:01,202
Their hunt leads from crashing a Boeing 747 into an Oslo freeport,

15
00:01:01,222 --> 00:01:04,197
to a chaotic highway heist in Tallinn.

16
00:01:04,247 --> 00:01:08,143
There, an inverted Sator captures the final piece of the Algorithm,

17
00:01:08,163 --> 00:01:10,693
and shoots Kat with an inverted bullet.

18
00:01:10,743 --> 00:01:14,167
To save her life, The Protagonist and Neil enter a turnstile,

19
00:01:14,187 --> 00:01:17,147
inverting themselves to travel backward in time.

20
00:01:17,197 --> 00:01:22,622
Meanwhile, Sator, who is dying of cancer, plans to end his life on his yacht in Vietnam,

21
00:01:22,642 --> 00:01:29,821
triggering a dead-man's switch that will bury the Algorithm forever at a Soviet-era blast site called Stalsk-12.

22
00:01:29,871 --> 00:01:33,772
Tenet launches a massive temporal pincer movement at Stalsk-12,

23
00:01:33,792 --> 00:01:37,777
attacking with forward-moving and inverted soldiers at once.

24
00:01:37,827 --> 00:01:43,979
While Kat stalls Sator on his yacht and kills him just after the Algorithm is pulled from the blast site,

25
00:01:43,999 --> 00:01:48,070
an inverted soldier takes a fatal bullet to save The Protagonist.

26
00:01:48,120 --> 00:01:52,168
Afterward, The Protagonist spots the orange trinket on Neil's bag.

27
00:01:52,218 --> 00:01:56,716
Neil reveals that a future version of The Protagonist recruited him years ago,

28
00:01:56,736 --> 00:02:02,450
and that he's going back to sacrifice himself. The Protagonist realizes he is the founder of Tenet,

29
00:02:02,470 --> 00:02:05,210
and the whole film was his own master plan.
